claim.claim-text:
an outer section (310) having substantially hollow interior;
an inner section (305) attached to a fuselage (106) of an aerial vehicle having a lesser chord length than the outer section (310) and configured to be stowed within the substantially hollow interior of the outer section (310) in a first configuration (102);
a telescoping means for extending the outer section (310) along a length of the inner section (305) to increase a wingspan in a second configuration (106), wherein the telescoping means is configured to expose the inner section (305) from the interior of the outer section (310) as the outer section (310) is extended along the length of the inner section (305); and
a control surface attached to a trailing-edge of the outer section (310), wherein the control surface attaches to the outer section (310) via a hinge (1215) mounted on an external surface of the trailing-edge.
